  "body": "## What changed\n\nEvery built-in post now writes three kinds of program comment, on by default:\n\n- the **setup** name, once, where its first section opens;\n- each **operation**'s name, kind and work offset, at its preamble;\n- each **tool**'s number, name, kind, diameter and corner radius, just before its tool call.\n\nPieces:\n\n- **Stream** (`crates/post/src/post/mod.rs`): four optional PARAMs, `OperationKind`, `SetupName`, `ToolKind` and `ToolCornerRadius`. Each is written only when it has a value, so a legacy stream or a user's .cps script that doesn't know them behaves as before. Documented in `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md`.\n- **App** (`posting::op_streams`): fills them from the operation's kind label, its effective setup, and the tool's kind and corner radius.\n- **Posts** (all seven under `assets/posts/`): a small, original \"comments\" block in each script. User text is cleaned per dialect: printable ASCII only, capped at 40 characters; `( ) % ;` become spaces, and Heidenhain also drops `*`. Every comment starts with our own keyword, so a user's name can't turn into an active comment such as LinuxCNC's `(MSG,`.\n\nSample lines:\n\n| Dialect | Comments |\n|---|---|\n| Fanuc / Haas / Mazak / Tormach | `(SETUP: Setup1)` `(OPERATION: Contour1 - 2D CONTOUR - G54)` `(T01 EM-0600-4FL - FLAT END MILL D6)` |\n| Sinumerik | `; OPERATION: Contour1 - 2D CONTOUR - G54` (unnumbered, like its machine-name line) |\n| Heidenhain DIN/ISO | `N10 ; OPERATION: Plane arcs*` (numbered block; no work-offset word, since this post selects the active preset) |\n| Fanuc lathe | `(T0101 TN-1600-0R8 - TURNING INSERT)` (no diameter for blades) |\n\nDecisions are recorded in `docs/decisions/257-gcode-comments.md`. The on/off post property is left to #258 / PR #302, which own the Post dialog. No UI is touched here.\n\n## Readings\n\n- 26 goldens regenerated (`WRITE_GOLDEN=1`). A script check confirmed only comment lines were added (50 in all): stripping them gives back each old file byte for byte. The one other change is Heidenhain's block numbers shifting. The 78 legacy `.cl` conformance goldens are unchanged, because their streams carry no PARAM or TOOL records.\n- `crates/post/src/post/mod.rs` was already 491 lines and is now about 518. Not split in this PR.\n\n## Pinning tests (`crates/app/tests/program_comments.rs`, new)\n\n- `every_mill_dialect_comments_the_setup_operation_and_tool_in_its_own_syntax`\n- `user_text_never_breaks_a_comment`\n- `a_stream_without_the_commentary_params_writes_no_comment`\n- `a_document_posts_its_setup_operation_kind_and_tool_kind`\n\nGate: `scripts/gate.sh quick` (macOS) green (post + app suites); ui lib tests that post (egui_app::tests, after_op_tests) green except the known `headless_run_succeeds`. 65 post-related test binaries pass (549 tests). clippy `-p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n\n## Needs a check on a real control\n\nEvery posted program changes. Before ready: a Hub / simulator run and a dry run on a real machine. The Heidenhain `N.. ; text*` form especially hasn't been tried on a TNC; the decision file names the fallbacks.\n\nChangelog: Posted programs carry comments naming the setup, each operation (name, kind, work offset) and each tool (number, name, kind, diameter, corner radius) in every built-in dialect's own comment syntax (#257)\n\nFixes #257\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
